 "caveats": [
  "Associations, not causes: the factors travel together and with things the data do not record.",
  "Coding differences between agencies and over time (results/quality_summary.json) can look like drivers; agency and sector x year controls absorb level differences but not coding that differs within an agency.",
  "Company ids changed when identifiers moved from DUNS to UEI in 2022, so incumbency is undercounted around that switch.",
  "Defense data arrive 90 days late; an incomplete Defense year is left out.",
  "Market depth is a count of companies registered in SAM.gov on one recent date, applied to every year; older years and retired NAICS codes fit it less well.",
  "Out-of-time log loss also moves with shifts in the overall single-offer rate between years; AUC (ranking only) is the steadier measure of how much a block explains.",
  "The sample gives each sector-year the same weight, so pooled effects are not dominated by the very many small Defense and GSA purchase orders; they describe that balanced mix, not every award equally."
 ],
